/-! # Normal arithmetic approximation of a smooth affine closed pair

Source: EGA IV4, Proposition 21.14.3(ii), arithmetic approximation in its proof;
IV3 7.8.3, 8.3.11, 8.5; IV4 17.7.8; IV2 6.1.4.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-normal-arithmetic-closed-pair-approximation)

The stages are indexed by a set of integer subalgebras, ordered by inclusion.
The affine schemes are represented intrinsically by `IsAffine`. The open-complement
stages are identified by open immersions whose images are exactly the complements.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A smooth affine closed pair over a Noetherian normal domain admits a directed
normal arithmetic approximation preserving fibre-component avoidance and generic
codimension at least two, with normal completed base local rings and limits of
both the affine schemes and their open complements.

Source: EGA IV4, Proposition 21.14.3(ii), arithmetic approximation paragraph.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-normal-arithmetic-closed-pair-approximation)

Proof:
1. By `lem-weil-pbc-smooth-algebra-finite-type-model`, descend the smooth algebra
   to a finitely generated integer subalgebra C. By
   `lem-weil-pbc-normal-finite-type-subalgebra-extension`, normal finitely generated
   integer subalgebras containing C form a nonempty directed system covering A:
   extend the algebra generated by two finite generating lists, or by one list
   and any specified element of A. Compatible ring maps glue uniquely on this
   union, giving its ring-colimit universal property. Smoothness persists by
   `lem-weil-pbc-smooth-ring-map-base-change-composition`.
2. The algebra B is Noetherian by `lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian`.
   Choose finitely many equations for Z and descend their finitely many tensor
   coefficients to one stage. Restrict to its directed tail. The tensor-pushout
   universal property `lem-weil-pbc-algebra-tensor-pushout-universal-property`
   identifies all subsequent closed pairs with base changes. The ring colimit
   of their coordinate rings is B. Apply `lem-weil-pbc-limit-affine-transition`
   to obtain the limiting cone with the displayed base-change projections.
3. Finite type over the integers makes the stages Noetherian by
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian`. Apply
   `lem-sfb-smooth-closed-fibre-codimension-locus` with c = 1 and then
   `lem-weil-pbc-limit-contained-in-constructible` to pass to a tail where every
   fibre avoids components. With c = 2, reflection under the fraction-field
   extension Frac(A_i) into Frac(A) gives the generic-fibre bound at each stage.
4. The integers are excellent by `lem-trf-integers-excellent`. Each stage local
   ring is excellent by `lem-exc-finite-type-localization-excellent` and normal
   by `lem-weil-pbc-localization-normal-domain`. Its completion map is regular
   by `def-weil-pbc-g-ring`, since localization at the maximal ideal is the same
   local ring. Its fibres are regular, hence normal by
   `lem-weil-pbc-regular-ring-normal`. The completion is Noetherian by
   `lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-noetherian` and flat by
   `lem-weil-pbc-local-completion-faithfully-flat`. Apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-flat-normal-fibres-noetherian-normal`. By
   `lem-weil-pbc-local-completion-local-ring` the completion is local, so this
   normality says it is an integrally closed domain.
5. The open complements are Noetherian and quasi-compact by
   `lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-open-subscheme-noetherian`, and quasi-separated by
   `lem-weil-pbc-locally-noetherian-quasi-separated`. Their transition maps are
   the restrictions of the affine transition maps, since each closed set is the
   inverse image of the earlier one. The open-restriction clause of
   `lem-weil-pbc-limit-affine-transition` gives affine complement transitions
   and the limiting cone with vertex the original open complement. -/
theorem normal_arithmetic_closed_pair_approximation
    {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsIntegrallyClosed A]
    [Algebra.FinitePresentation A B]
    [Smooth (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)))]
    (Z : TopologicalSpace.Closeds (Spec (CommRingCat.of B)))
    (η : Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) (hη : IsGenericPoint η Set.univ)
    (havoid : ∀ (t : Spec (CommRingCat.of A))
      (C : Set ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber t)),
      C ∈ irreducibleComponents ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber t) →
        ¬ C ⊆ (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι t ⁻¹' (Z : Set _))
    (hcodim : ∀ z : (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber η,
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι η z ∈ Z →
        2 ≤ ringKrullDim
          (((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber η).presheaf.stalk z)) :
    ∃ P : Subalgebra ℤ A → Prop,
      Nonempty {S : Subalgebra ℤ A // P S} ∧
      IsDirected {S : Subalgebra ℤ A // P S} (· ≤ ·) ∧
      Nonempty (IsColimit (CommRingCat.subalgebraCocone A P)) ∧
      (∀ i : {S : Subalgebra ℤ A // P S},
        i.val.FG ∧ IsIntegrallyClosed i.val ∧ IsNoetherianRing i.val ∧
        ∀ t : PrimeSpectrum i.val,
          IsDomain (AdicCompletion
            (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime t.asIdeal))
            (Localization.AtPrime t.asIdeal)) ∧
          IsIntegrallyClosed (AdicCompletion
            (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime t.asIdeal))
            (Localization.AtPrime t.asIdeal))) ∧
      ∃ (D E : {S : Subalgebra ℤ A // P S}ᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u})
        (f : D ⟶ (CommRingCat.subalgebraDiagram A P).op ⋙ Scheme.Spec)
        (p : (Functor.const _).obj (Spec (CommRingCat.of B)) ⟶ D)
        (Zi : ∀ i, TopologicalSpace.Closeds (D.obj i))
        (e : E ⟶ D)
        (q : (Functor.const _).obj
          (Scheme.Opens.toScheme (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of B)) Z.compl) ⟶ E),
        Nonempty (IsLimit (Cone.mk (Spec (CommRingCat.of B)) p)) ∧
        Nonempty (IsLimit
          (Cone.mk (Scheme.Opens.toScheme (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of B)) Z.compl) q)) ∧
        (∀ i, IsAffine (D.obj i) ∧ Smooth (f.app i) ∧
          LocallyOfFinitePresentation (f.app i) ∧
          IsNoetherian (D.obj i) ∧ CompactSpace (D.obj i) ∧
          QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i) ∧
          IsNoetherian (E.obj i) ∧ CompactSpace (E.obj i) ∧
          QuasiSeparatedSpace (E.obj i) ∧
          IsOpenImmersion (e.app i) ∧ Set.range (e.app i) = (Zi i : Set _)ᶜ ∧
          q.app i ≫ e.app i =
            (Scheme.Opens.ι (X := Spec (CommRingCat.of B)) Z.compl) ≫ p.app i ∧
          IsPullback (p.app i) (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)))
            (f.app i) (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom i.unop.val.val.toRingHom)) ∧
          (Z : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of B))) = p.app i ⁻¹' (Zi i : Set _) ∧
          (∀ (t : Spec (CommRingCat.of i.unop.val)) (C : Set ((f.app i).fiber t)),
            C ∈ irreducibleComponents ((f.app i).fiber t) →
              ¬ C ⊆ (f.app i).fiberι t ⁻¹' (Zi i : Set _)) ∧
          (∀ (ηi : Spec (CommRingCat.of i.unop.val)), IsGenericPoint ηi Set.univ →
            ∀ z : (f.app i).fiber ηi, (f.app i).fiberι ηi z ∈ Zi i →
              2 ≤ ringKrullDim (((f.app i).fiber ηi).presheaf.stalk z))) ∧
        (∀ (i j : {S : Subalgebra ℤ A // P S}ᵒᵖ) (a : i ⟶ j),
          IsAffineHom (D.map a) ∧ IsAffineHom (E.map a) ∧
          IsPullback (D.map a) (f.app i) (f.app j)
            (Spec.map ((CommRingCat.subalgebraDiagram A P).map a.unop)) ∧
          (Zi i : Set _) = D.map a ⁻¹' (Zi j : Set _)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
